From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tangenx <me@tangenx.dev>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:28:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 045/128] feat: clean tracking parameters from links

Full rule table from the tele desktop patch: a global rule (utm,
fbclid, gclid, spm and friends) plus per-provider rules for youtube,
spotify, twitter/x, instagram, threads, tiktok, facebook, reddit,
amazon (including /ref= path segments), aliexpress, vk, yandex,
google, linkedin, ebay, medium, github, steam, netflix, twitch, imdb,
bing, msn, apple, pinterest, hh.ru and ozon. Telegram hosts are never
touched.

Two toggles under privacy: opened links are cleaned in openClickableLink
(every message link goes through it), sent links are rewritten in
getEntities with entity offsets kept in sync. Defaults to off.

Constraint: only url/text-url entities are rewritten, code/pre spans are left alone
Rejected: cleaning on paste | needs the paste hook and a rules editor (0078/0079)
Confidence: medium
Scope-risk: moderate
Not-tested: needs a device pass with real tracked links
